RAG chatbot, here is a simple real-time example showing the difference.

1. Server-based real-time

Suppose you deploy your FastAPI + RAG application on an EC2 server.

                 SERVER-BASED
                     
User
 ↓
Frontend / Voiceflow
 ↓
FastAPI
 ↓
RAG
 ↓
Qdrant
 ↓
LLM
 ↓
FastAPI
 ↓
User

====

Example

Your EC2 server is running:

=========

from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.post("/chat")
def chat(query: str):

    # RAG processing
    documents = search_qdrant(query)

    # LLM processing
    answer = generate_answer(query, documents)

    return {"answer": answer}

====

The server is running continuously:

EC2 Server
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ FastAPI                  │
│ RAG                      │
│ Python                   │
│ Dependencies             │
└──────────────────────────┘
        ↑
        │ requests
        ↓
      Users

If 100 users send requests, the running server handles those requests.

Real-time means: the user sends a question and the already-running backend processes it immediately.

====

